{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal-record screening limits","requirement":"Before making a conditional offer, a housing provider may not inquire about an applicant’s criminal record. After the offer it may consider only qualifying convictions within set lookback periods, must make an individualized assessment, and may not require drug or alcohol tests.","key_value":"no inquiry before conditional offer; 6-year (1st degree), 4-year (2nd/3rd degree), 1-year (4th degree) lookbacks","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units is not a rental dwelling unit. A housing provider may still ask about methamphetamine-manufacture convictions in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex-offender registration.","penalty":"Director may impose up to $1,000 for a first violation, $5,000 with one prior violation in five years, $10,000 with two or more priors in seven years, plus cease-and-desist orders, compliance reporting, a remedy offer, and up to $1,000 paid to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application-fee disclosure requirement","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether criminal history is part of its eligibility criteria and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracy, rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units is excluded from the act.","penalty":"Upon a substantiated violation the director may require that the applicant’s rental application fee be returned, unless housing is provided to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction of former applicant after successful appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider’s appeal succeeds and the director’s decision is overturned, that determination is grounds to evict the former applicant housed under the director’s order, on at least 45 days’ notice before the eviction.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Former applicants who reside in a rental dwelling unit as the result of a director’s order, where the housing provider’s appeal succeeds and the court overturns the director’s final decision.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Applies only to a former applicant housed under a director's order"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"then a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Operates notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
